# Codex owns config.toml: it rewrites the file in place on every run, stamping in
# absolute paths ($CODEX_HOME, bundled-plugin paths under /Users/<you>) and a
# [projects."..."] trust entry per directory you visit. Symlinking it into this
# repo meant one machine's paths were pushed to every other machine, and the
# trust list grew by hundreds of entries that were pure churn in the diff.
#
# The file stays tracked as the reference copy of the *preferences* (model,
# reasoning effort, [features], approval policy) — copy those into a new
# machine's config.toml by hand. Everything else in ai/ is still stowed.
^/dot-codex/config\.toml$

# stow's built-in defaults, which naming this file would otherwise discard.
^/\.git$
\.gitignore
